      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for python311",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for python311 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-9669: crafted input can cause a stack buffer overflow (bsc#1267974).\n- CVE-2026-15806: urllib.request.HTTPPasswordMgr credentials for one URL scheme sent over another\n  scheme (bsc#1276223).\n- CVE-2026-17084: StringPrep algorithm considered Unicode codepoint attributes outside \n  Unicode 3.2.0 (bsc#1276226).\n\nChanges for python311:\n\n- Updated to version 3.11.16\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
